# Before syntax, a model

This is intentionally a **short demo lesson**. It exists so the application can be tested before the full curriculum is written.

C is often introduced as a collection of syntax rules. For this curriculum, that is not enough. We will treat every program as a claim about **objects, values, storage, lifetime and permitted operations**.

```callout
{
  "tone": "important",
  "title": "Course principle",
  "body": "Do not memorize a C expression before you can explain what objects it reads or changes, when those objects exist, and which assumptions make the operation valid."
}
```

## Source is not execution

Consider the following program.

```c
int main(void) {
    int x = 42;
    int *p = &x;
    *p += 1;
    return x == 43 ? 0 : 1;
}
```

At the source level we can already identify an integer object `x`, a pointer object `p`, the address-of operation, and an access through indirection. Later lessons would connect these concepts to compiler transformations, the C abstract machine, actual memory, ABI conventions and generated machine code.

| Layer | Question |
| --- | --- |
| C language | Is the program defined by the language rules? |
| Compiler | What transformations are legal? |
| ABI | How are values represented for this target? |
| Hardware | Which instructions and memory accesses occur? |

```memory
{
  "title": "Illustrative layout — not a language guarantee",
  "rows": [
    {"address":"0x7fff...a0","bytes":"2A 00 00 00","label":"x = 42"},
    {"address":"0x7fff...a8","bytes":"A0 ...","label":"p designates x"}
  ]
}
```

> A future full lesson will be much longer than this demo and will distinguish carefully between what C guarantees and what a particular machine merely tends to do.

```quiz
{
  "id": "q-machine-01",
  "type": "single-choice",
  "prompt": "Which statement is the safest starting point when reasoning about portable C?",
  "options": [
    {"id":"a","label":"Every C variable is always a visible RAM slot"},
    {"id":"b","label":"The C language defines semantics; a compiler may realize them in different machine-level ways"},
    {"id":"c","label":"A pointer is simply an unsigned integer"}
  ],
  "answer": "b",
  "explanation": "Portable reasoning starts from the language semantics. Concrete addresses, registers and instruction sequences depend on implementation and optimization choices."
}
```

```task
{
  "id": "task-machine-01",
  "title": "Explain the four layers",
  "detail": "In your own notes, write one sentence for language semantics, compiler, ABI and hardware. Do not copy the table."
}
```

## Transfer question

If an optimizer removes an apparent memory write, does that automatically mean the compiler violated the source program? Explain what information you would need before answering.
